From c1407e4cc0e7491de19ed4d47f42c6a302e0d998 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omesh <roland@nordhain.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Apr 2026 19:57:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 05/14] perf: parallel fast_refresh + hot-block diagnostics +
 corruption recovery
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- fast_refresh: after initial sequential pull_hashes, spawn up to 8
  parallel pull_hashes_extra calls using empty block_ids + start_height
  (DIRECT-BULK path, requires matching daemon support). HASH_BATCH=100k
  matches the daemon's maximum. fast_refresh drops from ~6min to ~40s.
- pull_blocks_extra: gap validation in parallel prefetch. Daemon returns
  variable block counts (size-limited), so subsequent batches at fixed
  heights can have gaps. Validate contiguity and discard batches after
  the first gap to prevent m_blockchain corruption.
- Added max_block_count parameter to pull_blocks_extra to hint daemon
  to return exactly batch_size blocks.
- process_parsed_blocks: detailed phase timing (cache_tx_data,
  generate_key_derivation, geniod, chain-integration) and per-block
  hot-block detection (>=10ms per block). Drill-down per-tx timing
  (>=1ms) inside hot blocks with txid, phase breakdown in
  process_new_transaction (unconfirmed_check/output_scan/input_scan).
- out_of_hashchain_bounds_error: when daemon's response start_height
  is ABOVE m_blockchain.size (corruption indicator), truncate chain
  to offset and re-fast_refresh instead of re-pushing the bad tip.
- fast_refresh: detect blocks_start_height > m_blockchain.size and
  abort cleanly to avoid pushing hashes at wrong indices.
- invoke_http_bin (epee): full HTTP-cycle instrumentation — request
  serialisation, HTTP roundtrip, gzip decompression, epee deserialise.

These changes unlock the ~5× faster cuprate fast-rpc node (tex8com/cuprate
fast-rpc branch) and give us the visibility to find further bottlenecks.
